---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | SwitchTape">
  <div class="legal-container">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Last updated: May 16, 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2>The Short Version</h2>
      <p>
        SwitchTape doesn't have user accounts. We don't have a user database. Your
        Spotify and Apple Music access tokens are stored only in your browser's
        localStorage — never on our servers. We do not track you, run ads, or use
        analytics or marketing pixels.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What We Access</h2>
      <p>
        When you connect Spotify or Apple Music, SwitchTape requests the minimum
        permissions needed for the feature you're using:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Playlist transfer:</strong> read access to the source playlist;
          write access to create a new playlist on the destination service.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Music Report Card:</strong> read access to your top tracks and
          artists (Spotify) or heavy rotation, recently played, and recommendations
          (Apple Music).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Where Your Data Goes</h2>
      <p>
        For <strong>playlist transfer</strong>, your music data flows directly between
        your browser and Spotify/Apple Music's APIs. SwitchTape's servers do not see
        or store your playlist contents.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the <strong>Music Report Card</strong>, your browser aggregates a small
        summary of your listening (genre counts, era breakdown, top artist names, etc.)
        and sends it to SwitchTape's server, which forwards it to
        <a href="https://ai.google.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Gemini API</a>
        to generate the personality report. The generated report is sent back to your
        browser and cached in your browser's localStorage. We do not retain the
        summary or the generated report on our servers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What We Store</h2>
      <p>
        On <strong>our servers</strong>: nothing about you. Our serverless functions
        process requests transiently — no database, no user records, no logs of your
        music data.
      </p>
      <p>
        On <strong>your device</strong> (browser localStorage):
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Spotify access and refresh tokens (so you don't have to log in every time)</li>
        <li>Apple Music developer token (cached for 24 hours)</li>
        <li>Your generated Music Report Card (so it's available offline)</li>
        <li>Your dark mode preference</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can clear all of this at any time by clearing your browser's site data
        for SwitchTape.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        SwitchTape does not set tracking cookies. We use browser localStorage for
        the items listed above, which is similar in spirit but doesn't get sent to
        any server automatically.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Third Parties</h2>
      <p>
        Three external services receive data when you use SwitchTape:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Spotify</strong> — see
          <a href="https://www.spotify.com/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Spotify's Privacy Policy</a>.
          Revoke access at
          <a href="https://www.spotify.com/account/apps/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">spotify.com/account/apps</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Apple Music</strong> — see
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>.
          Revoke access in your Apple ID settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Gemini</strong> (for AI report generation) — see
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
          Only the aggregated music summary is sent; no account identifiers are included.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        SwitchTape is hosted on Vercel. Standard Vercel access logs (IP address,
        request path, user agent, timestamp) are kept by Vercel for operational
        purposes per their privacy policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <p>
        Since we don't store personal data on our servers, there is nothing for us
        to export, modify, or delete on your behalf. To remove SwitchTape's access
        to your music accounts, revoke it directly with Spotify or Apple at the
        links above. To clear local data, clear your browser's site data for SwitchTape.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? Email
        <a href="mailto:justin@crispcode.io?subject=SwitchTape%20Privacy%20Question">justin@crispcode.io</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-container {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .last-updated {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 1rem 0 1rem 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--color-red);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  a:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
</style>
